  "summary": "The Art Deco style in Mumbai, India  is a notable feature of the architecture of the city.",
  "description": "The Art Deco style in Mumbai, India  is a notable feature of the architecture of the city.  It was used primarily for office buildings, residences and movie theaters, during a period when India was part of the British Empire. On 30 June 2018, an ensemble of such buildings were officially recognized as a World Heritage site by the UNESCO World Heritage committee held in Bahrain as the Victorian and Art Deco Ensemble of Mumbai.\n\nThe BBC reported that Mumbai has at least 200 Art Deco buildings in the city.",
